Description: Restore dedicated notification sockets for bonded LE clients
 A bonded client's CCC survives an ATT disconnect but its AcquireNotify IO
 does not. Remember which enabled CCC actually acquired an FD. Once the new
 ATT connection of that bond satisfies the CCC permissions, reacquire its
 IO, including when the phone sends no CCC write. An unsubscribe, disconnect
 or service removal invalidates pending replies. Count the subscription once.
 .
 Based on Ubuntu bluez 5.72-0ubuntu5.8. Includes upstream's per-client
 notification routing (a08ec1a4e93b7805cdda33600d83d946969acb47) and the
 disconnected-client IO selection fix from f7e2cd91c. Apply to the stock
 distribution source before building the bluetoothd package.
Forwarded: no

